-- C6-S1 follow-ups (roadmap rows 12, 13, 15, 17, 56 of cluster C6-COST-INFRA-SECURITY), charter pillar cost, program QNFO.INFRA.
-- The cost views and the qnfo-agents ledger rollup are in 2026-11-05-c6-s1-cost-views.sql. This file records what the slice did and did not close:
-- the last two unmetered Workers AI callers get a doer each (their files are claimed by other sessions), the Analytics Engine per-call write gets a
-- named owner, and each roadmap row gets the status its evidence supports. Nothing here adds spend.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'partial' WHERE id = 13 AND item = 'RM-COST-L6-DRAFT-VERIFY-1'; UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'partial' WHERE id = 15 AND item = 'RM-COST-PER-TASK-ALL-PATHS-1'; UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'partial' WHERE id = 17 AND item = 'RM-COST-FREE-FIRST-PARITY-1'; UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'not-built' WHERE id IN (12, 56) AND item IN ('RM-COST-L5-DISTILLATION-1', 'RM-ANALYTICS-ENGINE-METERS-1'); UPDATE agent_issues SET status = 'closed' WHERE title IN ('AI-METER-COVER-3a: qnfo-model-eval calls Workers AI with no attribution (6 call sites)', 'AI-METER-COVER-3b: qnfo-fleet-dashboard calls Workers AI with no attribution (2 call sites)', 'AI-METER-AE-1: Workers Analytics Engine data point per AI call (qnfo-agents, qnfo-code-orchestrator, qnfo-research-exec)') AND status = 'open';

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'AI-METER-COVER-3a: qnfo-model-eval calls Workers AI with no attribution (6 call sites)',
'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-model-eval/worker.js
code-anchor: async scheduled(_event, env, ctx) {
Pillar cost, program QNFO.INFRA, roadmap RM-COST-FREE-FIRST-PARITY-1. node scripts/ai_call_paths_audit.mjs (AI-CALL-PATHS-AUDIT-1) lists qnfo-model-eval as the benchmark worker that calls env.AI.run at 6 sites (probe and benchmark helpers) with no __aiAttrEnv wrapper and no ai_call_counters write, so none of its Workers AI spend reaches workers_ai_attribution_coverage_pct. Same defect and same fix as qnfo-email 2.12.5, qnfo-lifecycle 1.17.9 and the six workers of AI-METER-COVER-1 (agent_issues 1001705).
Fix: copy the WORKERS-AI-ATTRIBUTION-1 block (var __AI_ATTR_RATES and function __aiAttrEnv) verbatim from qnfo-gateway/worker.js to just after var VERSION, and make this the first line of both handlers (async fetch(req, env) and async scheduled(_event, env, ctx)): env = __aiAttrEnv(env, "qnfo-model-eval", "AI", "AUDIT"); (the qnfo-audit binding of this worker is AUDIT). Bump with python scripts/worker_release.py bump qnfo-model-eval. Add qnfo-model-eval/ai-meter.test.mjs modelled on qnfo-email/ai-meter.test.mjs. When it merges, delete the qnfo-model-eval line of UNMETERED_BASELINE in scripts/ai_call_paths_audit.mjs (a NOTE until 2026-11-12, a failure after).
Metric: workers_ai_attribution_coverage_pct (target >= 80). Prediction: +1 to +2 points (qnfo-model-eval is a small caller: the claim is attribution, not saving).
code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-model-eval/worker.js"], "contains": "__aiAttrEnv(env, \"qnfo-model-eval\", \"AI\", \"AUDIT\")"}',
'session:c6-s1', 'optimization', 'medium', 'open', CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000, CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title = 'AI-METER-COVER-3a: qnfo-model-eval calls Workers AI with no attribution (6 call sites)' AND status = 'open');

